#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/genutils/pinentry.xml:26
#, xml-text
msgid "Introduction to PIN-Entry"
msgstr "Introdução a PIN-Entry"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/genutils/pinentry.xml:29
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <application>PIN-Entry</application> package contains a collection of "
"simple PIN or pass-phrase entry dialogs which utilize the Assuan protocol as"
" described by the <ulink url=\"https://www.gnupg.org/aegypten/\">Ägypten "
"project</ulink>.  <application>PIN-Entry</application> programs are usually "
"invoked by the <command>gpg-agent</command> daemon, but can be run from the "
"command line as well. There are programs for various text-based and GUI "
"environments, including interfaces designed for "
"<application>Ncurses</application> (text-based), and for the common "
"<application>GTK</application> and <application>Qt</application> toolkits."
msgstr ""
"O pacote <application>PIN-Entry</application> contém uma coleção de caixas "
"de diálogos simples de entrada de PIN ou frase secreta que utiliza o "
"protocolo Assuan conforme descrito pelo <ulink url=\"https://www.gnupg.org/"
"aegypten/\">projeto Egito</ulink>. Os aplicativos <application>PIN-Entry</"
"application> geralmente são invocados pelo processo de segundo plano <command"
">gpg-agent</command>, mas podem ser executados a partir da linha de comando "
"também. Existem aplicativos para vários ambientes baseados em texto e GUI, "
"incluindo interfaces projetadas para <application>Ncurses</application> ("
"baseadas em texto) e para os kits comuns de ferramentas <application>GTK</"
"application> e <application>Qt</application>."

